rlands take 30% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["India: 11.2% ($5.9bn)","Spain: 9.3% ($4.9bn)","Netherlands: 9.3% ($4.9bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 30% of what Nigeria imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 29.8% ($13.0bn)","United States: 12.8% ($5.6bn)","India: 9.9% ($4.3bn)"]},{"headline":"2025 trade surplus of $11.7bn","detail":"Nigeria sells more than it buys. Surplus economies usually have foreign currency available, which makes getting paid and repatriating profit simpler.","angle":"risk","strength":"watch","evidence":["Exports $56.1bn vs imports $44.4bn in 2025","Exports moved 7.1% year on year"]},{"headline":"Early signal: live animals","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 294% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Agriculture & food: growing 294% a year since 2022, now 0.47% of imports at rank 31. Growth is uneven, so treat the projection as directional."]}]','2026-09-04 23:37:25'),('res_235b13e5842447c4991646','ent_kenya',NULL,'overview','{"year":2024,"export_usd":8255797029.967,"import_usd":20203122341.75,"balance_usd":-11947325311.783,"total_trade_usd":28458919371.717,"export_yoy_pct":15.334883083869725,"import_yoy_pct":8.592942519668537,"export_concentration":0.07645512049685264,"partner_count":182,"product_count":96,"services_export_usd":8044144072.40366,"services_import_usd":5638289796.69829,"data_sources":["un-comtrade","world-bank"],"coverage_note":null}','2026-09-04 20:04:36')