 22% of what Kenya imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 21.5% ($4.3bn)","United Arab Emirates: 12.6% ($2.5bn)","India: 9.8% ($2.0bn)"]},{"headline":"2024 trade deficit of $11.9bn","detail":"Kenya buys more than it sells. Deficit economies can face foreign-exchange shortages, so check currency availability and payment terms before committing.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $8.3bn vs imports $20.2bn in 2024","Exports moved 15.3% year on year"]},{"headline":"Services are a real part of this economy","detail":"Commercial services exports are $8.0bn, about 7% of GDP. That usually signals working payment rails, English or lingua-franca business capability, and buyers already used to contracting across borders.","angle":"entry","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Services exports $8.0bn against GDP $120.4bn in 2024"]},{"headline":"Early signal: metal ores & ash","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 69% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Minerals & energy — growing 69% a year since 2021, now 0.32% of imports at rank 41. Growth has been steady rather than a single spike."]}]','2026-09-04 20:04:36'),('res_91634c1b7df14ef69d91ca','ent_united-states','run_7586e7633b974979adbcc2','overview','{"year":2025,"export_usd":2177127769561,"import_usd":3504272131456,"balance_usd":-1327144361895,"total_trade_usd":5681399901017,"export_yoy_pct":5.491085137077867,"import_yoy_pct":4.392846787468026,"export_concentration":0.06962401664193416,"partner_count":196,"product_count":97,"services_export_usd":1232402000000,"services_import_usd":903282000000,"data_sources":["un-comtrade","world-bank"],"coverage_note":null